WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.480
- [Narrator] Here's how you
make a Cozy Cone Motel inspired

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:03.940
bacon mac and cheese cone at home.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.910
Start by rolling card
stock into a cone shape

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.160
and covering in aluminum foil,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.060
and coat with a non-stick cooking spray.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.580
Next, roll a package of pizza
dough into a large rectangle

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.160
and cut into one-inch strips.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.410
Starting at the point of the cone,

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.700
wrap the strips around.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.570
Coat with egg wash

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:20.340
and bake in a 425-degree
oven for 12 to 15 minutes.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.730
Next, the mac and cheese.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.140
Start by cooking a pound of pasta

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.600
according to the directions,

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.750
then cook your bacon and allow it to cool.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.250
Now onto the cheese sauce.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.890
Start by melting a 1/4 cup of butter

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.500
in a saucepan over medium heat

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.070
and then add a 1/4 cup of flour

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.910
and cook until golden and smooth.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.290
Then add two cups of milk

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:37.530
and whisk until smooth

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.300
and let the mixture
thicken over medium heat.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.850
Add 1/2 cup of cream
cheese, allowing to melt.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.750
Then eight ounces of
shredded cheddar cheese

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.350
and salt and pepper to taste.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.150
Stir until smooth.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:50.990
Add in your cooked noodles
and mix to combine.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.040
Fill your cones with the mac and cheese,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.350
top with the bacon,

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.060
and enjoy.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.950
Let's make some iconic Disney snacks.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.630
Here are my top five Disney recipes

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:01.090
you need to make at home.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.640
The Cheeseburger Pods from Pandora

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.800
are always one of my favorites,

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.380
and if you want a good
hack for this recipe,

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.490
you always can use flaky biscuits
from a tube for the buns.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.160
The Totchos from Woody's Lunchbox
are always a fan favorite.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.590
I mean, who doesn't love
chili over tater tots.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:14.670
I mean potato barrels.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:15.780
If you've ever been to Ohana,

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.530
you know how good the bread pudding is.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.164
It's easier to make at
home than you would expect,

00:01:19.164 --> 00:01:21.270
and you get to flambe, which sounds scary,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.320
but I swear it's not.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.083
I'm telling you now,

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.050
if the spring roll cart
in Magic Kingdom is open,

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:27.770
you best believe you can find me there.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:28.850
I'm making the pepperoni ones,

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.970
but I also have the recipe
for the cheeseburger ones,

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.630
so take your pick on what you like.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:33.800
They come together really quick,

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.020
and you also can make
these in the air fryer.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:36.853
And finally,

00:01:36.853 --> 00:01:39.080
my favorite snack slash
meal in all of Disney World.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.660
I have recipe tested
this one so many times,

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.710
and I think I have come
close to perfection

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.140
to making the Ronto Wrap at home,

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:45.973
so check it out.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.360
Here's how you make
the cheddar cheese soup

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.060
from Le Cellier in Epcot.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.250
This recipe is pretty simple.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.980
We're starting off by
frying up some bacon.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.210
And to that, we're adding
celery and red onion.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:56.070
Once that's cooked,

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.060
we're going to add in
some flour for thickness.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.060
As always, the full recipe will be posted

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.420
over on my Instagram.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.490
Then it's just a process.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.570
We're adding some chicken
stock, letting that simmer.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.650
I know that Le Cellier is
technically a steakhouse,

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.830
but I think this is probably
the most famous dish

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:09.663
on their menu.

00:02:09.663 --> 00:02:11.040
Once that's simmered down and thick,

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.450
we're adding in some milk.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.480
The creaminess of the soup
will really come together

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.310
in the last 15-minute simmer.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.440
You can't have cheddar cheese
soup without cheddar cheese.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.690
We're adding in eight ounces
of shredded cheddar cheese.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:22.230
I prefer to shred my own.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.300
I just think it gives it a
better texture in the soup.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.530
And then it's your final spices,

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:28.300
which is Tabasco,
Worcestershire, salt, and pepper,

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.133
and it's Canada,

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:31.470
so we're finishing it off
with a 1/4 cup of beer.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.563
Be sure to follow along for
even more Disney Parks recipes.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:36.600
Do you recognize this snack?

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.920
Let's head over to Magic Kingdom

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.390
and recreate one of my
all-time favorite sweet treats,

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.670
the Cheshire Cat Tail.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.120
We're starting this recipe on the stove

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.280
with some milk and vanilla,

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.380
and we're just heating that up.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.660
We're making an easy creme pat.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.960
The whole recipe will be
posted over on my Instagram

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.230
if you have any questions.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.090
But then we're just taking
eggs, sugar, and corn starch,

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:53.923
giving that a mix.

00:02:53.923 --> 00:02:56.650
And then we're slowly adding
the heated milk mixture

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.850
back into the eggs, just
so we don't scramble them.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.110
It's called tempering.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.460
And that goes back on the stove

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:02.700
until it gets thick and bubbly.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.830
Then we're just rolling out
some frozen puff pastry,

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.140
we're topping it with that creme pat,

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:08.670
and then we're also topping
it with mini chocolate chips.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.610
This is my favorite sweet
treat in Magic Kingdom.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:11.880
It usually has its own stand,

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.800
but right now, you can
find it at Cosmic Ray's.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.650
Then we're just holding it
over, essentially like a book,

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.100
and then we're just going to cut it

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.490
in one and a 1/2 inch section,

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.270
pop them in on
parchment-lined baking sheet,

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.103
give them a twist,

00:03:22.103 --> 00:03:24.520
and bake them in a 400-degree
oven until golden brown.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.850
Once cooled, it's time to ice,

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.410
and that's just powdered sugar, milk,

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:28.560
and a bit of food coloring.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.650
Use a spoon to drizzle,

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.630
and you've gotten yourself
a Cheshire Cat Tail

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:32.653
from Magic Kingdom.

